# What Cloud Build uploads.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which excludes the
# private baselines -- correct for a public image, and wrong for a run
# meant to include them. This file exists so the choice is explicit
# rather than a side effect of version control.
#
# It deliberately does NOT exclude concrete_baselines/_private_*.py:
# the image is pushed to a private Artifact Registry, and a benchmark
# run that omits half its algorithms is not the run that was asked for.
# Note this names no method -- it excludes by pattern, like .gitignore.
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, "benchmarks/" matches at
# any depth -- including scripts/benchmarks/, which holds the
# Dockerfile, so the build failed with "no such file or directory" on
# its own build context.
/runs/
/benchmarks/
/docs/envs/
/docs/environments/
*.gif
.DS_Store
